<section class="page-header">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h1>Everything in one space</h1>
    <p>The pieces most teams stitch together from four or five separate tools, built to work as one.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="feature-list-section">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="feature-group">
      <h2>Write and organize</h2>
      <div class="feature-list">
        <div class="row">
          <h3>Documents</h3>
          <p>
            A real rich-text editor with headings, lists, tables, images, embedded video, code, and
            checklists. Editing is live and multiplayer, with your teammates' cursors on the page, so
            a document updates as your team types, not after they save.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <h3>Spreadsheets</h3>
          <p>
            A full spreadsheet grid with formulas, kept in the same folders as your documents instead
            of a separate app.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <h3>Collections</h3>
          <p>
            Structured collections with named, typed fields and records, for lists that need more shape
            than a spreadsheet.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <h3>File manager</h3>
          <p>
            Folders and documents organized the way a file system works, with pinned items for what
            you open most, so a Space stays navigable as it grows.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-group">
      <h2>Track the work</h2>
      <div class="feature-list">
        <div class="row">
          <h3>Tasks</h3>
          <p>
            Every checklist item in a document is a task, linked straight back to where it came from.
            Work through them as a backlog or a kanban board, with subtasks, start and due dates.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <h3>Epics and initiatives</h3>
          <p>
            Group tasks into epics and epics into initiatives, each with its own progress rolled up
            from the tasks underneath.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <h3>Sprints</h3>
          <p>
            Time-boxed sprints with a goal and dates. Assign tasks to a sprint and filter the task
            list by it.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <h3>Calendar</h3>
          <p>
            A list or month view of everything with a due date, without leaving your Space for a
            separate calendar app.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-group">
      <h2>Plan ahead</h2>
      <div class="feature-list">
        <div class="row">
          <h3>Milestones</h3>
          <p>
            Target dates that roll up progress from every initiative, epic, and task linked to them,
            and flag themselves on track, at risk, or off track.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <h3>Hierarchy</h3>
          <p>
            One tree from milestone to initiative, epic, task, and subtask, with a progress bar at
            every level and anything unassigned gathered in one place.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <h3>Roadmap</h3>
          <p>
            Initiatives and their epics in one lane per milestone on a shared timeline, plus a
            Now / Next / Later board for work that doesn't have dates yet.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <h3>Gantt chart</h3>
          <p>
            Task and epic bars on a timeline with milestone markers and a today line. Link tasks
            with dependencies, drawn as arrows, and highlight the critical path driving the finish.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <h3>Goals and OKRs</h3>
          <p>
            Objectives with key results and a score. A key result tracks a number by hand, or follows
            the progress of the initiative it's linked to.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-group">
      <h2>Work together, anywhere</h2>
      <div class="feature-list">
        <div class="row">
          <h3>Spaces</h3>
          <p>
            A Space for each team, with members as viewers, members, admins, or owners, plus a
            personal Space that's just yours.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <h3>Sharing</h3>
          <p>
            Send a read-only link to any document. Whoever opens it doesn't need an Inertia account.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <h3>Native apps</h3>
          <p>
            The same Spaces as a native Mac app and on iOS, alongside the web version, not a second
            product with its own quirks.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <h3>Light and dark</h3>
          <p>
            The app follows your system's light or dark setting, and so does this site.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="cta-section">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="cta-row">
      <a class="btn" href="/signup">Get started free</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
